tasks/BACKLOG.md:492:✅ **F-WIN-2 — THE KIT-VS-BOSS GUARD HAS NO CODE FACT TO STAND ON, AND THAT IS AN OWNER RULING (lane-a 2026-09-02, drained s2457).** Split out of the lane's combined `F-WIN-1 / F-WIN-2` row so it carries its own declaring subject rather than riding inside another finding's (the F-1328-3 shape — caught by `desk-declaration-guard` in my own closing battery, F-1300-4). **F-WIN-1 is the RECEIPTS half and it SHIPPED**: 36 door contracts published where the task and spec say 39, `e1-drill-yard` admitted but rejected by `functions/api/standings.ts` (`practice.standings:false`) and so recorded `unclaimed / standings-disabled`. **F-WIN-2 is the GUARD half and it is PARKED, by the master's own honesty clause.** The requested invariant — *no contract may field a boss its starting kit cannot hurt* — cannot be expressed truthfully against today's runtime: `HeadlessContractSim.ts:819` says the Steamworks arsenal is not a floor or grant and a virgin profile leaves all three shooters disabled, `Game.ts:1563` gates them on research plus the Baron medal, yet `CombatSystem.ts:891` routes ordinary bolts into every live enemy and `Enemy.ts:774` gives the railcar no immunity. **So removing `twist.pressureEnabled` cannot make a literal "can damage" guard red, and the E2 mutation proof the master demanded has nothing to measure.** **GATE — attended ruling picks the invariant: (a)** add a real standalone pressure-arsenal floor in a separately scoped balance/grant slice and guard THAT, or **(b)** define "can hurt" as generic projectile damage and replace the mutation proof. **rec (b) first** — it is honest about what the runtime does today and costs one small slice; (a) is the larger design statement and can follow. **Do not encode `pressureEnabled` as an arsenal grant while the runtime says it is not one.** ⚖️ **Nothing is broken and nothing waits on this: the receipts half stands alone and shipped at `b5850417ad05b1e870d8fda8866a86f32bf400b1`.** Review: `reviews/winnability-receipts.md`. **IMPLEMENTED on lane-a, awaiting drain:** `scripts/kit-guard.test.mjs` executes the real `CombatSystem` bolt/blast paths plus `Enemy.takeDamage` for all 36 door contracts (84 contract-kind paths, 46 distinct rows); current table is uniform except the authored non-zero E2 bolt scales. Mutation proof: a temporary `rail_tough` immunity reded all four contracts that field it, then greened after revert. ✅ **SHIPPED s2466 at `adacf5e131fcec6df1496671129961e0468a1a46` — THE GATE ABOVE IS DISCHARGED: option (b) is implemented, gated and merged.** Review: `reviews/kit-guard-generic-damage.md`. Gated in detached worktree `gate-s2466`; the gated tree and main's merge tree are the same object `b436a743a`, so what shipped is byte-identical to what was measured. Evidence: tsc clean · build green · `test:node-guards` **607 tests / 602 pass / 0 fail / 5 skipped, rc=0 in 1264.8 s run ALONE** · `test:power-budget` p95 0.329 ms · `test:task-guards` PASS. **Teeth re-derived independently of the runner (F-2462-3):** a `rail_tough` immunity reds exactly `e2-hill-mine`/`e2-incline`/`e2-pressure-garden`/`e2-trestle`, reproducing the runner's mutation proof contract-for-contract. ⚠️ **BUT THE COVERAGE CLAIM IN THE CLAUSE ABOVE IS CORRECTED BY MEASUREMENT: the asserting set is 31 door contracts, not 36 — see F-2466-1.** **Option (a), a standalone pressure-arsenal floor, is UNCHANGED and still open as a later balance slice.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:506:⛔ **F-WIN-1 / F-WIN-2 — S1 WINNABILITY GUARD STOPPED ON ITS HONESTY CLAUSE (lane-a, 2026-09-02).** The receipts half is implemented and live-regenerated: `public/skill.md` publishes **36** door contracts, not the task/spec's 39; four currently have a verified current-lineage secure and 32 are unclaimed. `e1-drill-yard` is one of the 36 but `functions/api/standings.ts` rejects it by construction (`practice.standings:false`), so its receipt is explicitly `unclaimed` / `standings-disabled`. The guard half cannot be written truthfully from the named code: `HeadlessContractSim` says the Steamworks arsenal is **not a floor or grant** and a virgin profile leaves all three shooters disabled; `Game` likewise gates them on research plus the Baron medal. Conversely, `CombatSystem` routes ordinary bolts into every live enemy and `Enemy.takeDamage` has no railcar immunity, so removing `twist.pressureEnabled` cannot make a literal "can damage" guard red. The requested E2 mutation proof therefore has no code fact to derive. **GATE:** attended ruling chooses the invariant: (a) add a real standalone pressure-arsenal floor in a separately scoped balance/grant slice, then guard that floor; or (b) define "can hurt" as generic projectile damage and replace the pressure-floor mutation proof. Do not encode `pressureEnabled` as an arsenal grant while the runtime says it is not one.
