tasks/BACKLOG.md:1135:🟢 **F-2247-1 + F-2247-2 (s2247 2026-08-23, FOUND AND CURED THE SAME FIRE ON A DRY BOARD — THE INHERITED CORPUS-vs-CLAIM AXIS, TAKEN AND LIVE ON ITS FIRST SUBJECT. GATE: none — this row is a completion.)** 🧭 **THE INHERITED AIM WAS TESTED BEFORE IT WAS SPENT ON, AND IT PAID ON THE FIRST INSTRUMENT.** s2246 handed forward one question — *is the subject set as wide as the sentence the tool prints next?* — and explicitly retired the five-tool census that preceded it. Applied to the SIX gate legs reached by `npm run` alias (a population any "bare legs" census misses by construction), `citation-title-guard` is the MODEL and is banked SOUND: it prints *"This verdict covers `tasks/**` only"* IN the verdict and names the `2,123` citations in `219` tracked `.md` it does NOT gate, citing the owner scope ruling F-1252-1. **A tool that states its own scope in its verdict is what the cured ones below now do.** 🎯 **F-2247-1 — `ruling-propagation-guard`, chained bare in `test:ledger-guards`. Its verdict is defined by ROLE — *"no REFUSAL cites a finding the owner has already ruled"*, universal over refusals — while its subject test was SIX EXACT KEY SPELLINGS.** 📊 **MEASURED on the live tree: `17` of the `44` refusing leaves (**38.6%**) carry NONE of the six, so the scan joined an EMPTY string and was structurally incapable of redding on them whatever they said — **38,681 chars of refusal prose unread, 13 of the 17 citing an F-id.** The tree holds **138** reason/note spellings, and the guard was reading `closedReason` (4 uses or fewer) while ignoring `closureReason` (24), `drainNotes` (172), `note` (160) and `authorNotes` (146) — **the three commonest reason-bearing keys in the entire tree.**** 🔑 **THE PROVENANCE IS THE SHARPEST PART: this file's own comments say it MIRRORS `drain-block-check.mjs`, and it does — for the terminal-status set, and for the leaf definition, where the comment calls the fidelity *"load-bearing"*. It mirrored its sibling in two places out of three and stopped at the one that decides WHAT IT READS.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND NOT INFLATED: LATENT. Every hit I read resolved to a citation, not a basis, so today's PASS was TRUE — verified, not assumed. What earns it a row is that the blindness lands in a GATE, in the permissive direction, in the DEFAULT mode the battery uses.** 🛠️ **CURE: widen to the spellings whose NAME states the refusal BASIS (+8, including session-stamped variants — `stoppedNote_s1263` and `stoppedNote` are one record, the anchoring mistake s1249 already paid for), and DECLARE the residue always, including the happy path (F-2208-1). Residue **17 → 5**, each named on stdout; the PASS sentence now reads *"no READABLE refusal…"* whenever anything went unread.** 🚦 **WHY NOT THE FULL WIDENING, AND THE BOUNDARY IS MEASURED RATHER THAN STYLISTIC — this is the half a weaker cure gets wrong: scanning the narrative fields (`note`, `drainNotes`, `authorNotes`) reds on THREE live leaves and **ALL THREE REDS ARE FALSE.** `b4v2-picnic-stake-pressure` and `vp-02e-jumper-8way-activation` each RECORD that a ruling was propagated (*"(F-2085-1 RULED)"*, *"OWNER RULING PROPAGATED s1655"*), and `lane-vp-02b-jumper-slot-red`'s drainNotes REFUTES the citation outright (*"It is NOT -- F-1166-1 … treats this spec as GREEN"*). **In a narrative field an F-id is as likely to be a refutation or a propagation record as a basis.** Redding there would turn this guard's OWN remedy text — *"say so without naming the ruled finding"* — into an instruction to DELETE propagation records, i.e. to corrupt correct bookkeeping under the Retention Law, and a guard that fires on ordinary correct work is excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1). **So the 5 that remain DECLARE AND DO NOT RED** (F-2218-1's restraint). 🎯 **F-2247-2 — AND IT IS WHY "IMPORT THE SIBLING" WOULD HAVE SHIPPED THE SIBLING'S DEFECT.** `drain-block-check`'s resolver excludes retired reasons by naming ONE spelling, `priorBlockedReason`; the tree holds **SIX** (`priorStoppedReason`, `priorStopNote_s1206`, `priorStopNote_s1288`, `priorBlockReason_s1110_SUPERSEDED`, `priorBlockClass`). Worse, the survivors rank FIRST: `priorStoppedReason` matches its closure-stem test on *"stop"* while the live `closureReason` does NOT — **so a retired reason OUTRANKED the real one.** 📊 **MEASURED: `2` of the `42` terminal-closed leaves resolved to `priorStoppedReason` (`agent-rung-honest-gate`, `ap-06b-panel-ladder-and-voice`), and BOTH carry a `closureReason` stating the actual supersession. `agent-rung-honest-gate`'s own `authorNotes` warns IN WORDS — *"READ THIS BEFORE THE PRIOR REASON BELOW, WHICH THE RULING OVERTURNS"* — and the instrument picked exactly the overturned one.** That is precisely the harm the file's own comment describes for `priorBlockedReason` (*"printing that as the closure cause would be WORSE than silence"*), reached by a spelling the exclusion did not cover. **Exclude the CLASS, not the member.** ✅ **NEUTRAL BEFORE LANDING (F-1274-2), control asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1 — *"pre-cure arm produced 154 B, rc 0 — it really ran"*): `ruling-propagation-guard` is verdict- and rc-neutral (still PASS, rc 0) over a corpus **12 leaves wider**; `drain-block-check` is byte-identical in 4 of 5 modes, and the ONE divergence is the intended correction, rc unchanged.** 🔒 **`scripts/refusal-reason-corpus-guard.test.mjs` — 13 arms, 0.9 s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`.** 🔬 **TEETH, every variant manufactured on a scratch copy whose edit ASSERTS ITS ANCHOR APPLIED: PRE-CURE both files reds **9 of 13** (7 from the guard, 2 from the sibling), and each over-general cure is caught by exactly the reverse control built for it — scan-the-narrative-fields reds the propagation-record control · declare-only-on-failure reds the happy-path arm **ALONE** · widen-but-leave-the-verdict-unqualified reds the scope arm **ALONE** · exclude-every-reason-ish-key reds the "must not swallow a legitimate closure reason" control.** ⚠️ **TWO OF MY OWN ARMS WERE LYING AND THE SWEEP CAUGHT BOTH — this is the method lesson and it cost the fire its most useful half-hour.** (1) The pre-cure arm reddened with the FILE PATH as the test name, not a test name: the pre-cure copy does not export the symbols the cure adds, so the suite died at MODULE LOAD and reddened **9 arms while testing nothing.** A missing export is a CONSTRUCTION failure, not evidence about the defect; the imports of added symbols are now LAZY, so a pre-cure copy still loads and the arms testify behaviourally. (2) The arm named *"declares on the HAPPY path"* asserted through the CLI — but `main()` is `import.meta.url`-anchored, so **no fixture can drive the live board to `unreadable === 0`**, and the arm passed identically against a declare-only-on-failure variant. **It was asserting the happy path from a board that has never been happy.** The decision is now extracted and exercised directly, WITH a separate arm on the call site (F-2209-1: extracting a decision to make it testable creates a new untested seam). 🔭 **REACHABILITY AUDIT DISCHARGED (s2226's duty) AND IT EARNED ITS KEEP FOR THE THIRD FIRE RUNNING: after seven variants, `2` of 13 arms had reddened NOWHERE — both reverse controls on the retired/authoring exclusions. The variant that reaches them is the one a next fire is most likely to WRITE: adopt the sibling's stem match wholesale WITHOUT carrying its exclusions. It reds 7 arms including both. All 13 now red somewhere.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it sharpens the inherited axis rather than merely confirming it: s2246 said a subject test that admits by FORMAT under a claim defined by ROLE is the shape. **The correction is that WIDENING THE FORMAT IS NOT THE CURE — measured here, the full widening manufactures three false reds and turns the guard's remedy into an order to destroy evidence.** When the claim is a ROLE, ask which FIELDS PLAY THAT ROLE — a basis, a record, a refutation and an intent are four different things wearing one shape — then widen to the role and DECLARE the rest. And when a file says it MIRRORS a sibling, check WHICH PARTS: this one mirrored the status set and the leaf definition and not the corpus, and the sibling it would have imported was itself defective in the same direction.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1268:🔺 **F-E2F-2 (attended 2026-08-22, OWNER — non-blocking; raised by `reviews/e2-finished.md`, desked s2163): THE PRESSURE LINE IS NOW OPTIONAL ON BOTH STEAMWORKS MAPS.** With E2 admitted at `3366c65f7`, the `dry` control — a rider who declines the pressure line **entirely** — secures on **all four bench seeds** (`b7a0e199`, `ca203296`, `3984671c`, `3fbcf331`, all w14). Steam is now **available rather than required** on the railcar pair. **This is not a defect and nothing is blocked** — the epoch still teaches pressure on the Hill Mine and the Pressure Garden, and the review says so plainly. ❓ **THE OWNER QUESTION, AND IT IS A DESIGN ONE, WHICH IS WHY NO FIRE MAY SETTLE IT:** if the intent is that the Steamworks maps must be won *with* steam, the cadence is the dial to tighten — at the cost of one railcar configuration. ⚠️ **DO NOT ACT ON THE REVIEW'S NUMBERS FOR THAT REMEDY — SEE [F-2163-1]:** it reads *"0.75 → 0.8 on the trestle"*, and the trestle **ships 0.7** while **0.8 is the rung its own table labels `← last failing rung` (0 of 4)**, so the literal remedy would de-admit the map. The remedy matching the stated cost is **0.7 → 0.75** (trestle), whose sole failure is `railcar-02 ✗ w13`. **Cost if ruled "steam must be required": one number per contract, one re-run of the admission battery. Cost if ruled "leave it": nothing — the shipped state IS the leave-it state.** Filed as its own row because the guard is right that a mention inside the E2 row is not a declaration (F-1328-3).
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1272:🔎 **F-2163-1 (s2163 2026-08-22, ATTENDED/TUNER-OWED — A REMEDY THAT, READ LITERALLY, WOULD DE-ADMIT THE MAP IT IS MEANT TO TIGHTEN).** `reviews/e2-finished.md`'s **F-E2F-2** — the one finding of the four addressed to the OWNER — ends *"(0.75 → 0.8 on the trestle would restore that, at the cost of the seed-02 railcar config)"*, and **both numbers disagree with the same review's own trestle ladder four paragraphs above.** 📐 **MEASURED BY READING THE TABLE, not inferred:** the trestle **SHIPPED 0.7** (42.9s, ALL FOUR) — not 0.75; **0.75 is its 3-of-4 rung**, whose sole failure is `railcar-02 ✗ w13`, which is *exactly* the parenthetical's stated cost; and **0.8 is the row the table itself labels `← last failing rung`** (turrets-01 ✗ w14, railcar-01 ✗ w10 = **0 of 4**). ⚠️ **So the remedy read literally moves the trestle to a rung that secures NOTHING — de-admitting the map the merge just admitted and reversing E2's 4/4 claim.** The remedy consistent with the cost clause is **0.7 → 0.75**. (`0.75 → 0.8` fits neither map: the INCLINE ships 0.75, but its 0.8 rung is ALL FOUR, so there it costs nothing at all.) ✅ **NOTHING SHIPPED IS WRONG AND NOTHING IS BLOCKED** — the merged cadences are the tables' own shipped rungs (trestle 0.7 / incline 0.75) and E2's admission stands; only the owner-facing remedy SENTENCE is mis-numbered. That is why it is filed rather than fixed here: the cost of a mis-numbered dial is paid by whoever acts on it, and the actor is Robin. 🚫 **NOT FIXED BY THIS FIRE, DELIBERATELY:** `reviews/e2-finished.md` belongs to the attended writer who was live at filing time (one-writer-per-surface, CLAUDE.md §4.4); the fix is one sentence. ⓘ The GZ-01 item filed this fire for `3366c65f7` states the F-E2F-2 owner choice **without** the numbers for this reason. ✅ **EXECUTED (attended 2026-08-22 — the review’s own writer): `reviews/e2-finished.md`’s remedy sentence re-numbered to `0.7 → 0.75`, the correction recorded in place. The F-E2F-2 desk row above already carries the corrected numbers.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1289:🟢 **E2 IS FINISHED — BOTH RAILCAR MAPS THROUGH THE DOOR, THE EPOCH 4/4 (2026-08-22, headless Opus agent on `worktree-agent-a383c2ed5dd452ebd`, base `4b7883cf0`; PROPOSED, not yet drained).** Owner, verbatim: **"yes, I want to admit it, E2 should be finished as well"** — approving [F-1608-2]'s priced `hpScale` 30 → 12.5 railcar cut and stating the intent. 🪜 **A FOUR-STEP PROGRAMME, EACH STEP MEASURED ALONE BEFORE THE NEXT WAS TAKEN:** ⑴ the pressure LINE (2026-08-21) → arsenal fires, neither secures · ⑵ the COAL, `twist.coalSeams` (2026-08-21) → fuel delivered doubles, neither secures · ⑶ the RAILCAR CUT (this ruling) → **measured to change NOTHING** · ⑷ the CADENCE, `twist.waveCadenceMult` → **both maps secure on every path**. ⭐ **STEP 3 IS THE FINDING [F-E2F-1]: A BOSS-HP DIAL CANNOT REACH A CLAIM THAT NEVER MEETS THE BOSS.** Applying the ruled cut ALONE and re-running the exact blocking configs returned **byte-identical event logs** — `e6fe4301`, `74a94d27`, `17116d57`, `2207a312` — because the railcar spawns at wave 12 and those claims died at 6 and 10. It moves the one run that DOES reach the boss (`096a69c6`→`80f9f5fb`) and could never have been sufficient alone. **Had it shipped together with the cadence, the programme would have credited the wrong dial and carried a false balance belief forward. RULE: when a ruling names a dial, ship it alone first and measure it alone.** 📏 **THE KNIFE-EDGE LADDERS (Stillwater method; every rung = both bench seeds × both best-play configs, so "ALL FOUR" = 4/4 secured).** **Trestle:** 1.0 ✗ · 0.9 ✗ · 0.8 ✗ · 0.75 3-of-4 · **0.7 ALL FOUR ← SHIPPED** · 0.65 ALL FOUR · 0.6 ✓. **Incline:** 1.0 ✗ · 0.95 2-of-4 · 0.9 2-of-4 · 0.85 2-of-4 · 0.8 ALL FOUR · **0.75 ALL FOUR ← SHIPPED** · 0.7 ✓ · 0.6/0.5/0.4 ✓. ⚖️ **The two numbers differ because the maps were judged INDEPENDENTLY and each got its own measured minimum** — first all-secure rung 0.75 (trestle) and 0.8 (incline); each ships ONE CLEAR RUNG INSIDE that, with securing rungs on both sides. Never more than the measured minimum, never on the edge. ✅ **THE ADMISSION BATTERY: 32 rows, every one identical across two passes, 24 secured = all 12 non-idle rows ×2.** trestle-01 `fnv1a32:514cfcc2`/`fnv1a32:0d12b7b6`/`fnv1a32:b7a0e199` · trestle-02 `fnv1a32:4ca66057`/`fnv1a32:0228df25`/`fnv1a32:ca203296` · incline-01 `fnv1a32:8ba7f716`/`fnv1a32:de405e9d`/`fnv1a32:3984671c` · incline-02 `fnv1a32:eaca8451`/`fnv1a32:cf55d4ed`/`fnv1a32:3fbcf331` (line/deep/dry), all w12–w14. **Law 2 holds: all four idle floors terminate UNSECURED at wave 1.** 📚 **FULL ADMISSION TEMPLATE:** both exemption rows **REMOVED** (5→3, removed not reworded — the secure now exists); door list 33→**35**; census flips to all four E2 ids, per-id and explicit ([F-1660-1]'s lesson), and now ASSERTS both rulings (the railcar pair must declare 3 seams + its own cadence; hill-mine and pressure-garden must declare NEITHER); `null-floors.json` regenerated to **77 pairs, both maps gain honest w1 rows, and ZERO pre-existing floors moved** — hill-mine `4b3cd37b`/`6a1b7941` byte-unmoved, proved by diffing the pre-regen artifact. The full ladder derivation lives at `ContractFamilies.ts`'s `waveCadenceMult` declaration, because `contracts.json` is strict JSON and cannot carry a comment. 🔺 Raises [F-E2F-2] (**the pressure line is now OPTIONAL — the dry control secures on all four seeds**; if Steamworks maps must be won WITH steam, the cadence is the dial to tighten — OWNER, non-blocking) and [F-E2F-3] (the incline's 0.85–0.95 band is genuinely bistable, not measurement noise — read it as a cliff between two viable openings). Closes [F-1608-2]. Review `reviews/e2-finished.md`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1296:🟡 **E2 COAL MOVES ONTO ITS OWN CLAIM, AND THE REASON THE OWNER NEVER FOUND IT (2026-08-21, headless Opus agent on `worktree-agent-a383c2ed5dd452ebd`, base `d775fca71`; PROPOSED, not yet drained).** TWO owner items in one slice. ⑴ **RULING** to the [F-E2PL-1] lever, verbatim **"sounds like a good idea"**: `coalSeams` is now a lawful twist key — added to `AUTHORED_TWIST_KEYS` with schema validation that refuses an empty list, a placeless seam, and coal on a contract declaring no `pressureEnabled` (nothing could burn it). `PressureSystem` reads `twist.coalSeams` and falls back to the exported `DEFAULT_COAL_SEAMS`; **both engines read it through one identical expression** (`Game.ts:1538`, `HeadlessContractSim.ts:821`). `e2-trestle` authors three seams along its mine spur (mean **29.4wu** from its stake) and `e2-incline` three in its lower yard (**28.8wu**), against the Hill Mine's measured **29.4** standard and the **55/58wu** they paid before. 📊 **THE LEVER WORKS — AND NEITHER MAP CONVERTS IT.** Pressure delivered DOUBLED (192→368 trestle, 192→384 incline; incline lance fires 164→288), the incline ceiling moved w9→w10, and across **96 runs on the new coal the only secure is still the run that DECLINES the line** (`dry-e2-trestle-02` w18 `bc515b13`). Both exemption rows STAY, reworded. 🔒 **ZERO-CHANGE PROVED TWICE:** `e2-hill-mine-01` reproduces `fnv1a32:c40556c0` after every edit, and all four dry controls reproduce their pre-ruling hashes **with the seam coordinates moved**; idle floors unchanged (w2/w1/w2/w2); audit summary unmoved at 468/1090/4, 6 exemptions. ⑵ **PLAYTEST REPORT** (owner, verbatim: *"I was not able to ever obtain coal or use the pressure weapons when I played maps in E2"*) — **INVESTIGATED, NOT ASSUMED. The coal was never buried:** every lump on all three maps measures **gap 0.000** against the sculpted ground, both viewports, and 0.8s standing on one yields its 4 coal. ⭐ **And the reason it escaped F-SEAM-1 is a real difference worth keeping: `GoldNode` places once at spawn and needed the `resampleVisualHeights` hook; `PressureSystem.syncSeams()` re-samples EVERY FRAME, so it is self-healing — its absence from that list is CORRECT and must not be "fixed"** ([F-E2CS-3], now a comment on the extended guard). 🎯 **WHAT ACTUALLY STOPPED HIM: the Hill Mine's briefing never mentioned coal.** It named the terraces, the switchbacks and the flooded gallery, while `e2-pressure-garden`'s card had said *"The coal seams cluster on the highest terrace above the boiler beds"* all along — one map in the epoch taught it, and the one he meets first did not. The coal is also **off-camera from the stake** (29wu north) and the lump reads as ambient scatter. ✅ **CURE SHIPPED — the missing sentence, in the house voice, on the three cards that lacked it**, pinned in `contract-briefings.spec.ts` so it cannot rot back out. Acceptance frames for the owner at `artifacts/e2-pressure-line/coal-shots/` (briefing → coal seen → coal cut, desktop + 390px). 🔺 Raises [F-E2CS-1] (the lump reads as scenery — OWNER: art brightening vs nerfing `coal_survey`), [F-E2CS-2] (the VIEW carries no coal — an agent cannot locate it through the public grammar; fire-authorable, the F-E3CF-5 shape), [F-E2CS-4] (**the trestle's only remaining lever is now [F-1608-2]** — 384 pressure and 46 shots reach the hpScale-30 railcar and it lives). Review `reviews/e2-coal-seams-and-legibility.md`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1304:🟡 **THE E2 PRESSURE LINE REACHES THE LAST TWO RAILCARS — OWNER RULING EXECUTED, BOTH MAPS RE-PROVED, BOTH STILL REFUSE THE DOOR (2026-08-21, headless Opus agent on `worktree-agent-a383c2ed5dd452ebd`, base `789dc39a7`; PROPOSED, NOT yet drained).** Owner verbatim: **"E2's pressure ... - lets do that"**, executing the standing REC on [F-E2PA-6], *"give both the pressure line"*. ✅ **THE RULING IS NOW DATA:** `assets/contracts/epoch-2-steamworks/contracts.json` gains **two lines** — `"pressureEnabled": true` on the `e2-trestle` and `e2-incline` twists, placed exactly as the two siblings declare it. **Nothing else moved: the `hpScale: 30` railcar, the rosters, the spawn gates, the build zones and `secureWave` are untouched** — the ruling gives the player the ARSENAL, not a nerf. ⚖️ **REJECT-DON'T-STRETCH, STATED OUT LOUD (Mistake #14):** the task asked for *"the boiler/coal/site fields the siblings declare"* and **there are none** — `PressureSystem.ts:23` fixes the three coal seams as a MODULE constant on every map, and `ContractFamilies.ts:1542`'s `AUTHORED_TWIST_KEYS` is a hard allowlist that **throws** on any other pressure key. `pressureEnabled` is the entire vocabulary; both tiles already named their boiler ground in `stakeMarkers` years ago. 📊 **158 MEASURED RUNS — 154 THROUGH THE PROVER, EVERY BATTERY ROW ×2, ALL 24 IDENTICAL BOTH PASSES.** The gift is real and delivered: boiler house on both boards, **3/3 coal seams reachable on both maps** (12 vents each), arsenal firing on real pressure — **192** spent on the incline (164 lance / 2 mortar / 1 rocket), **317** on the trestle (37/14/14). **And nothing secures:** trestle w12 `7ee055ee` / w13 `ca23df0e`; incline w6 `dc7cf546` / w9 `66a4df57`. The single secure in the whole programme is the run that DECLINES the line (`e2-trestle-02` w18 `bc515b13`) — the same seed-02-only split the pre-ruling review measured. ⭐ **THE ATTRIBUTION ROW IS THE LOAD-BEARING ONE:** a rider that ignores the new line reproduces the previous review's pre-ruling hashes **bit for bit on all four bench seeds** (`8c28f1ff` / `bc515b13` / `83b0a873` / `dac0c325`, ×2 each) — **the contract edit is provably inert until a boiler burns coal.** 🗺️ **WHY THE MAPS STILL WIN, MEASURED:** the fixed seams sit **29wu** from the Hill Mine's stake but **55wu** from the trestle's only hero stake and **58wu** from the incline's, and the Prospector is the same single body that earns every coin — so on these two maps the pressure line is bought with the economy that buys the guns. The incline is not close for a different reason again: wave 6/9 with the hero at 2 HP and two turrets, four spawn edges onto a stake it cannot leave; there, coal timing is provably irrelevant (schedules `9,10,11`, `11,12,13` and `99,99,99` return the *identical* hash — the run ends first). ✅ **BOTH EXEMPTION ROWS STAY, REWORDED FROM THE DEAD REASON TO THE MEASURED ONE** (the `e6-showroom` / `e3-fairground` shape); door unchanged at 30; audit summary unchanged at 504/1016/4 with 8 exemptions (four rows flip in place to `advertises BUILD boiler_house`, all `equal`); `null-floors.json` regen moves **one byte — `eraStamp`** ([F-E2PL-4]: already stale on main before this branch existed), **not one floor**, and idle with pressure declared still builds nothing (w2/w1/w2/w2 on the previous review's own hashes). Plain-boot probe **4/4** across both contracts × desktop + 390px mobile, walking the real board-launch path and asserting the resolved `contract.activeId`, `pressure.enabled: true`, 3 seams, **0** boilers built. 🔺 Raises [F-E2PL-1] (owner fork — contract-authored coal seams, the smallest change that could plausibly admit either map) and re-prices [F-1608-2]; discharges [F-E2PA-6]'s fork. Review `reviews/e2-pressure-line-railcars.md`; evidence + prover + probes preserved at `artifacts/e2-pressure-line/`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1306:🔺 **F-E2PL-1 (OWNER FORK, OPEN — raised 2026-08-21 by the E2 pressure-line slice; NOT yet on the OWNER'S DESK because a fire may not edit STATUS line 1 — owed to the next attended window)** — **THE COAL SEAMS ARE A MODULE CONSTANT, AND THAT IS WHAT ACTUALLY HOLDS THE LAST TWO E2 MAPS OUT.** `src/systems/PressureSystem.ts:23` hard-codes the three seams at `(-12,39)`, `(-5,43)`, `(3,39)` — the same three coordinates on every contract in the game — and `ContractFamilies.ts:1542`'s `AUTHORED_TWIST_KEYS` allowlist **throws** on any per-tile alternative, so no contract can move them. Those coordinates were chosen for the Hill Mine's minehead: **29wu from its stake, 55wu from the trestle's, 58wu from the incline's.** Measured this slice: the seams ARE reachable on both maps (3/3 cut, boilers burning, 12 vents each) — the walk is simply not repaid, because the same single body earns all the gold. ➡️ **THE FORK: author a contract-level `coalSeams` list (defaulting to today's three when absent) so the Trestle can put its seams on the north approach and the Incline in its upper ore yard · or leave the seams where the fiction puts them and rule the two maps elite-accept.** ⚠️ **Why it is the owner's and not a fire's:** it changes `PressureSystem` for all four E2 maps (the Hill Mine and Pressure Garden pins move), and *where the coal is* is a canon question as much as a balance one. ⚖️ **Sizing it honestly: this is the smallest change that could plausibly turn EITHER map into an admission** — but it would likely move only the TRESTLE, since the Incline dies at wave 6 of 12 long before any boss. Sibling of [F-1608-2] (the `hpScale` 30 → 12.5 cut); both are what survive [F-E2PA-6]'s discharge. Measured in `reviews/e2-pressure-line-railcars.md`. ✅ **RULED AND EXECUTED (owner, 2026-08-21, verbatim: "sounds like a good idea").** `coalSeams` is now a lawful twist key (`AUTHORED_TWIST_KEYS`, schema-validated, refuses an empty list and refuses coal on a contract with no `pressureEnabled`); `PressureSystem` reads it and falls back to `DEFAULT_COAL_SEAMS`. Both railcars author three seams on their own ground — trestle mean **29.4wu**, incline **28.8wu**, against the Hill Mine's measured **29.4** standard and the **55/58wu** they paid before. 📊 **THE LEVER WORKS AND DOES NOT ADMIT EITHER MAP:** pressure delivered DOUBLED (192 → 368 trestle, 192 → 384 incline; incline lance fires 164 → 288) and the incline ceiling moved w9 → w10, but across 96 runs on the new coal the only secure is still the run that DECLINES the line (`dry-e2-trestle-02` w18 `bc515b13`). Both rows STAY, reworded to the new ceiling. 🔒 **Zero-change proved twice over:** `e2-hill-mine-01` reproduces `fnv1a32:c40556c0` after every edit, and all four dry controls reproduce the pre-ruling hashes **with the seam coordinates moved**. ➡️ **THE TRESTLE'S ONLY REMAINING LEVER IS NOW [F-1608-2]** — 384 pressure and 46 arsenal shots reach the `hpScale: 30` railcar and it lives. Raises [F-E2CS-1] (the lump reads as scenery — owner: art vs research nerf) and [F-E2CS-2] (the VIEW carries no coal; fire-authorable). Review `reviews/e2-coal-seams-and-legibility.md`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1465:🔬 **F-2114-1 (s2114 2026-08-21, DRY BOARD — A DESK ROW CAN BE DISCHARGED *BY CODE*, AND NO INSTRUMENT ON THIS BOARD COMPARES THE DESK TO `src/`. F-E2S-3 IS CARRIED AS 1 OF 29 ITEMS "AWAITING A WORD"; ITS RULING WAS EXECUTED IN FULL AND ITS CENTRAL PREMISE IS EXPLICITLY REFUTED IN A MERGED REVIEW FILE.)** 📋 **WHY THIS RUN EXISTED.** s2113 closed the alarm-row queue and wrote *"the next sweeper needs a NEW selection rule, not the next item on this list."* Board re-measured, not inherited: six queues EMPTY · `tasks/running/` EMPTY · no `CODEX-WALL` · assayer EMPTY · newest `tasks/failed/` **2026-08-11** · newest done-move already `drained-`/`stopped-`-prefixed · no `src/`/`e2e/` dirt · runner pid 451 alive. Nothing to drain and I did not manufacture one. 🔑 **THE NEW SELECTION RULE: not "which row sounds alarming" but "which row's ANSWER already exists somewhere no instrument reads."** The desk records a QUESTION; the ledger records the question's STATE; **the code records whether it was answered** — and nothing joins the third to the first two. 🎯 **THE SUBJECT.** `tasks/BACKLOG.md` F-E2S-3 opens **"RULED: de-list now, socket later … FIRE-AUTHORABLE, two masters, the de-list first."** That is not a desk row at all by its own text — the owner's word was GIVEN, and what remained was authoring. ✅ **BOTH HALVES SHIPPED, MEASURED BY EVALUATING THE DOOR RATHER THAN READING ABOUT IT** (`supportedContractIds()` loaded through vite SSR, the `gr-sim.test.mjs:150` pattern): the live door admits **29** contracts — `e2-trestle` **NOT ADMITTED**, `e2-incline` **NOT ADMITTED**, `e2-pressure-garden` **ADMITTED** exactly as the ruling required it stay, and `e2-hill-mine` **ADMITTED**. The "socket later" half is `c74a6c258` (*"E2 pressure arsenal headless — Hill Mine re-admitted via declared progression, exemptions 6→5"*): `PressureArsenalSystem` now constructs in `HeadlessContractSim` on the browser's own four gates, none relaxed. **`e2-hill-mine` is admitted because it SECURED on both bench seeds** (w15 `fnv1a32:c40556c0`, w16 `fnv1a32:9625a071`, each ×2) with a **cold control** proving a gate and not a grant (same policy, same seeds, no declaration → 576 pressure burned, **zero weapons fired**). `door-admission-ratchet` **GREEN** this fire: *"derived door matches the fixed admission baseline"* — today's shape is the sanctioned one. ⛔ **AND THE ROW'S PREMISE IS REFUTED IN WRITING, ON MAIN, BY THE SLICE THAT SUPERSEDED IT.** F-E2S-3's proof reads *"THE BOARD SELLS NO WEAPON THAT CAN TOUCH THE RAILCAR … minimum killing kit: nonexistent — cost infinite."* `reviews/e2-pressure-arsenal-headless.md` answers it by name: *"F-E2S-3 said 'no weapon reaches the railcar' and inferred the board sold no such weapon. **It sells three.**"* 🕳️ **WHY EVERY INSTRUMENT READS IT AS LIVE, AND THIS IS THE DURABLE HALF.** `desk-state-audit` joins desk ↔ `BACKLOG.md` ↔ `goals.json` and **never opens `src/`**; its verdict here is `OPEN-DESK-ONLY`, which is the *normal resting state* of a live desk item (**28 of 29**), so a discharged row and a live one are **indistinguishable by construction**. `authorable-candidates` is blind from the other side: its own header calls the `planned` goal leaves *"the factory's whole authorable-candidate surface"*, so **ruled, fire-authorable work parked in a desk row is invisible to the very instrument every dry-board fire cites** — the F-1654-1 shape, one surface further out. ⚖️ **SCOPE, STATED HONESTLY: I checked 2 of 29 against code, not 29.** All 29 rows were read and all 29 resolve to real BACKLOG rows (no ghosts). ✅ **THE CONTROL MATTERS AS MUCH AS THE HIT — THE RULE DISCRIMINATES:** F-E8LO-3 checked the identical way is **STILL LIVE**, `src/town/worldDispatches.ts:56` reading `'M8-5': { kind: 'boss', id: 'e8-low-orbit' }` exactly as its row claims. A sweep that flagged everything would be worthless. 🔗 **RETIRING F-E2S-3 LOSES NO LIVE QUESTION, WHICH IS WHY IT IS SAFE:** the surviving fork — *should the trestle and incline run a pressure line, or fall to turrets alone?* — **already has its own desk row, F-E2PA-6**, and the review states the measured reason both stay out (neither declares `twist.pressureEnabled`, so the arsenal has no fuel against an `hpScale: 30` railcar). F-E2S-3's desk presence was duplication of a settled matter. 🚫 **NO MECHANISM IS PROPOSED, DELIBERATELY.** "Has this row been answered in code?" is a JUDGEMENT, not a lookup — a red guard on it would fire on every open fork and be excused into uselessness within a week (the `cross-engine` label's fate, F-1460-1; the same reason F-1665-1 declined its own guard). The cure is the selection rule, applied by a reader. ➡️ **THE REUSABLE LESSON: a desk is a QUEUE OF QUESTIONS, and questions are answered by events its own instruments cannot observe. When a row has sat for hundreds of fires, do not ask "is this still open?" — ask "WHERE WOULD THE ANSWER HAVE LANDED, and has anyone looked there?"**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1471:🔬 **F-2108-1 (s2108 2026-08-21, DRY BOARD — A DESK ROW'S HEADLINE WAS REFUTED ON MAIN SIXTEEN HOURS BEFORE THIS FIRE AND THE ROW STILL ASSERTS IT; ITS s2072 VERIFICATION HAS ROTTED IN BOTH HALVES; ITS ATTENDED-OWED GATE IS DISCHARGED TWICE OVER; AND WHAT SURVIVES IS THE SAME QUESTION AS TWO OTHER DESK ROWS THAT HAVE NEVER BEEN LINKED TO IT.)** 📋 **WHY THIS RUN EXISTED, AND THE METHOD IS s2107's.** s2107's priority (C) generalised its own win into a search: *"when a row predicts its own figure will rot and says nothing is watching, that sentence is a dated alarm — go set it off"*, and named the phrases to grep. I ran that grep across all 29 carried desk rows at the BACKLOG line numbers `desk-state-audit` resolves for each: **13 of 29 carry at least one alarm phrase.** Ranked by cost, the cheapest was **F-1608-2** at 2,014 chars, carrying both *"nobody has"* and *"silently"*. 🎯 **THE FIGURES IT FLAGGED ARE INTACT — AND THAT NEGATIVE RESULT IS WHAT AIMED THE REST OF THE FIRE.** F-1608-2's claim is that the Hill Mine Baron's `hpScale` was cut 30 → 12.5 while Trestle Run and The Incline retain 30, and it cites a count and two coordinates. **Re-measured on main: `hpScale": 30` returns exactly 2, at `assets/contracts/epoch-2-steamworks/contracts.json:418` and `:810`, the two coordinates the row names — no rot in count and none in coordinate**, and the hill mine sits at `12.5` at `:182`. ⓘ **HITS CONTROLLED BEFORE THEY WERE BELIEVED:** the four top-level contract ids sit at `:6` `e2-hill-mine`, `:270` `e2-trestle`, `:478` `e2-pressure-garden`, `:640` `e2-incline`, so `:418` is inside the trestle and `:810` inside the incline — the two maps the row names, confirmed by containment rather than assumed from order. 🔑 **SO THE ROT WAS NOT IN THE NUMBER — IT WAS IN THE SENTENCE NEXT TO IT.** F-1608-2's reassurance reads *"Both maps are currently door-de-listed **per F-E2S-3**, so nothing is blocked meanwhile"*, and that clause has a history: it was **VOID for ~15 hours** when `48a0d41ab` turned the door into a derivation and dropped the ruling (F-1660-1), and was restored s1662 `25499e0a1` with a fixed-denominator ratchet *"so a future derivation cannot drop a ruling silently"*. **The ratchet held and the de-list is intact — but the ATTRIBUTION is dead**, and following it is what found the real defect. 🚨 **F-E2S-3's HEADLINE IS REFUTED ON MAIN, AND THE ROW STILL CARRIES IT.** The row (`:625`) is titled *"PROVEN BY THE SOL CRACK EXPERIMENT — e2-hill-mine IS UNSECURABLE HEADLESS BY CONSTRUCTION: THE BOARD SELLS NO WEAPON THAT CAN TOUCH THE RAILCAR"*. **`19dd85c0a` (merge, 2026-08-20T13:08:46, code `c74a6c258` at 12:51 — SIXTEEN HOURS BEFORE THIS FIRE) refutes it in terms**, and `reviews/e2-pressure-arsenal-headless.md:24` says so by name: *"F-E2S-3 said 'no weapon reaches the railcar' and inferred the board sold no such weapon. **It sells three.**"* Its evidence table: `e2-hill-mine-01` **SECURED w15**, 535 kills, `fnv1a32:c40556c0`, arsenal firing lance/mortar/rocket **29 / 14 / 12**; `e2-hill-mine-02` **SECURED w16**, 627 kills, `fnv1a32:9625a071`, **68 / 29 / 23**. ⭐ **And the load-bearing row is the COLD CONTROL** — identical policy and seeds with no declared profile: **0 / 0 / 0 weapons fired**, 432 and 576 pressure burned to nothing, unsecured w17/w18. That is the discriminator that makes it a gate rather than a grant, and it is exactly the control this factory's own law asks for. 📉 **s2072's IN-TREE VERIFICATION HAS ROTTED IN *BOTH* HALVES — MEASURED FIRST-HAND BY EXECUTING THE MODULE, NOT BY READING IT.** The row asserts *"verified s2072 in the tree — `e2-hill-mine`/`e2-incline`/`e2-trestle` all sit in `CONTRACT_ADMISSION_EXEMPTIONS` **each citing `F-E2S-3`**"*. I loaded `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts` through vite SSR and asked it: **exemptions are now 7 — `e2-incline, e2-trestle, e3-fairground, e5-stillwater, e6-showroom, e7-relay-rush, e9-seed-run`.** ⑴ **`e2-hill-mine` is GONE: `exempt=false, admitted=true`, and it appears in `supportedContractIds()` (29 ids).** The map F-E2S-3 declared unsecurable by construction is **through the door**. ⑵ **Neither survivor cites F-E2S-3** — both carry `citation: reviews/e2-pressure-arsenal-headless.md`. **So the sentence is false in its count AND false in its citation**, and the desk row that rests on it (F-1608-2) inherits the second error. ✅ **AND THE GATE F-E2S-3 LEAVES BEHIND IS DISCHARGED TWICE OVER.** Its NEW GATE reads *"attended spec for the Layer-2 socket; one owner word retires this row from the desk"*, and its §📌 says what remains is *"a separately scoped Layer-2 pressure-arsenal socket using campaign-carried progression, which needs a SPEC before any master may be authored (§2E)"*. **⑴ The spec exists and names this row: `specs/epoch-saga/e2-railcar-pressure-socket.md`, status line `RATIFIED 2026-08-13 … **fixes F-E2S-3** · buildable now`. ⑵ Its cure then SHIPPED** — the review's own summary is *"the browser's `PressureArsenalSystem` now exists in `HeadlessContractSim`, constructed on the browser's own four predicates and not one relaxed"*, with progression **declared** through the campaign harness (`gr-sim-campaign.mjs:88`), which is the *campaign-carried progression* the row asks for by name. **The row's remaining ask was answered before the row was last read.** 🔗 **WHAT ACTUALLY SURVIVES IS ONE OWNER QUESTION WEARING THREE DESK ROWS — AND NO ROW NAMES ANOTHER.** All three are live on the 29-item desk right now: ⓐ **F-E2S-3** (`:625`) — residue: the two railcar maps stay de-listed. ⓑ **F-1608-2** (`:456`) — *should Trestle Run and The Incline get the hill mine's 30 → 12.5 cut?* ⓒ **F-E2PA-6** (`:81`) — *"THE FORK: give both the pressure line (REC) vs leave them measured-only."* **The arsenal review poses ⓑ and ⓒ as a single sentence** (`:24`): *"should the trestle and incline claims run a pressure line, or is their railcar meant to fall to turrets alone?"* — the first clause is F-E2PA-6, the second is F-1608-2, and F-E2S-3 is the row that made them de-listed in the first place. **This is the s2106 shape (F-1501-3 + F-1640-1, adjacent 454 handoffs and never once linked) at THREE rows instead of two.** ⚖️ **THE TWO GROUNDS, STATED HONESTLY SO THE OWNER IS NOT OVER-SOLD.** The live exemption reason holds the pair out on two independent terms: ⑴ **neither declares `twist.pressureEnabled`** — measured, that key appears exactly twice in the E2 contracts, `:134` (hill mine) and `:574` (pressure garden), so trestle and incline can build no boiler, burn no coal, and the E2 arsenal has nothing to spend; ⑵ **both field a railcar at `hpScale: 30`** against the hill mine's 12.5. **F-1608-2's cure moves term ⑵ ONLY, so ruling it alone would NOT re-admit either map** — which is precisely why the three collapse into one question rather than three independent ones, and why answering them separately would waste two of the owner's words. 🚫 **WHAT I DID NOT DO, EACH REFUSAL LOAD-BEARING. ⑴ I closed no desk item and the desk stays 29** — only the owner's word closes an owner-desk row (§7.3), and F-E2S-3's own text reserves that word. **⑵ I did not edit a line of code** — not the exemptions table, not the contracts, not a citation string; re-admitting or re-tuning a map is the owner's fork by all three rows' own gates. **⑶ I did not author a master** — the live question is a design fork, which §2E's HARD LIMIT forbids authoring against. **⑷ I did not re-run the arsenal battery**: the securing evidence above is **quoted** from the review, not re-measured by me. **What I measured first-hand is the DOOR** — and the door is the half that the stale sentence got wrong. 🔒 **HONEST LIMITS. ⑴** I did not verify that hill-mine still secures *today*; I verified that main **admits** it, which is the claim F-E2S-3 contradicts. **⑵** The 13-of-29 alarm census is keyed on `desk-state-audit`'s resolved line numbers, so a desk item whose row moved since that resolution would be miscounted; the three rows I acted on were each re-anchored and proved **present and unique** before use. **⑶** I did not audit the other 10 alarm-carrying rows — they are named below for the next fire, unswept. 💡 **THE REUSABLE HALF, AND IT SHARPENS s2107's RULE RATHER THAN REPEATING IT: THE ALARM PHRASE FINDS THE ROW, BUT THE ROT IS OFTEN NOT IN THE FIGURE THE ROW FLAGGED — IT IS IN THE ATTRIBUTION SITTING BESIDE IT.** F-1608-2 flagged a number and guarded it well; every figure it cites is intact to the coordinate. What decayed was the four words *"per F-E2S-3"* — a pointer to **why**, which no ratchet watches, which no figure sweep would have checked, and which was the thread that led to a refuted headline, a doubly-rotted verification and a discharged gate. **A row can be perfectly right about its numbers and stale about its reasons, and the reasons are what the owner actually rules on.** Corollary: **when a row cites another row as its reassurance, re-read the CITED row — the reassurance is only as live as the thing it points at.** Related: [F-1608-2], [F-E2S-3], [F-E2PA-6], [F-E2S-4], [F-1660-1], [F-2072-1], [F-2107-1], [F-1501-3], [F-1640-1], [F-DOOR-4].
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1558:🔺 **F-E2PA-6 (OWNER FORK, OPEN — declared s2083; id minted here because the fork was recorded in prose with no key)** — the E2 arsenal merge (`19dd85c0a`) rewrote the **trestle and incline exemptions to measurement** and authored **no pressure economy on either**. **THE FORK: give both the pressure line (REC) vs leave them measured-only.** Same provenance as F-CAP-2: recorded in the five-merge window row, carried to the desk s2083, GAZETTE item filed. ⚠️ Minting the id is deliberate — an owner fork with no key cannot be tracked by `desk-state-audit` or declared to any guard, so it silently ages; if the attended author prefers a different id, rename it and keep the row. 🔗 **THIS IS THE ROW THAT STATES THE LIVE FORK, AND TWO OTHER DESK ROWS ARE ASKING THE SAME QUESTION — LINKED s2108 (F-2108-1).** `reviews/e2-pressure-arsenal-headless.md:24` poses the whole thing in one sentence: *"should the trestle and incline claims run a pressure line, or is their railcar meant to fall to turrets alone?"* — **the first clause is this row; the second is [F-1608-2]** (*should Trestle Run and The Incline get the hill mine's `hpScale` 30 → 12.5 cut?*, figures re-measured intact s2108); and **[F-E2S-3]** is the row that de-listed all three maps in the first place, whose headline is now **refuted** and whose attended-owed gate is **discharged** — so its residue is this fork and nothing else. ⚖️ **The pair is held out on TWO independent grounds and this row moves only one of them:** neither map declares `twist.pressureEnabled` (that key appears exactly twice in the E2 contracts, `:134` hill mine and `:574` pressure garden), **and** both field a railcar at `hpScale: 30` against the hill mine's 12.5. **Granting the pressure line without the difficulty ruling leaves an ~8× railcar in front of a freshly-fuelled arsenal; granting the cut without the line leaves an arsenal with nothing to spend.** ➡️ **REC: answer all three here in one word** — this row's id is the one to keep, per [F-E2S-3]'s own retirement rec. See [F-2108-1]. ✅ **ANSWERED AND EXECUTED (owner, 2026-08-21, verbatim: "E2's pressure ... - lets do that" — the REC branch, "give both the pressure line").** Both contracts now declare `twist.pressureEnabled: true` (`assets/contracts/epoch-2-steamworks/contracts.json`, +2 lines, nothing else touched). **MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED — and the answer is that this row's clause alone does NOT re-admit either map, exactly as [F-2108-1] predicted it would not.** The gift is real: boiler house on both boards, all three coal seams reachable on both maps (3/3 cut, 12 vents each), arsenal firing on real pressure (192 spent on the incline, 317 on the trestle). But across **154 prover runs** — a 130-run best-play search over 7 ladders × 2 upgrade orders × up to 4 coal schedules × 4 bench seeds including 6 pre-ruling controls, plus a 24-run ×2 battery (94 runs on the trestle, 60 on the incline) — **exactly one run secured, and it is the one that IGNORES the pressure line** (`e2-trestle-02` w18 `fnv1a32:bc515b13`). ⚖️ **THE CAUSE IS GEOMETRY THAT NO CONTRACT CAN AUTHOR, AND IT IS THE NEW FACT ON THIS FORK:** `src/systems/PressureSystem.ts:23` fixes the three coal seams at three literal WORLD coordinates on every map, and `AUTHORED_TWIST_KEYS` has no key to move them. Those coordinates were placed for the Hill Mine's minehead — **29wu from its stake, but 55wu from the trestle's only hero stake and 58wu from the incline's** — and the Prospector is the same single body that earns every coin, so fuelling the arsenal is bought with the economy that buys the guns. 🔒 **THE EDIT IS PROVABLY INERT UNTIL A BOILER BURNS COAL:** a rider that declines the new line reproduces the pre-ruling review's own hashes bit for bit on all four bench seeds (`8c28f1ff` / `bc515b13` / `83b0a873` / `dac0c325`, ×2 each) — no balance moved, and the `hpScale: 30` railcar is untouched per the ruling's own scope. ➡️ **SO THE SURVIVING HALF IS [F-1608-2] PLUS A NEW SIBLING [F-E2PL-1]** (contract-authored coal seams). **This row's fork is CLOSED; it may leave the OWNER'S DESK** — a fire may not edit STATUS line 1's desk, so the retirement is owed to the next attended/drain window. Review `reviews/e2-pressure-line-railcars.md`.
