 tavernkeeper-e10 300K/131.3/131.2/131.3 · clerk-e5 300K/141.3/137.3/139.3 · clerk-e6 300K/143.2/141.0/142.1 · clerk-e7 303K/142.4/137.3/139.9 · clerk-e8 297K/142.8/138.1/140.4 · clerk-e9 309K/125.9/124.1/125.0 · clerk-e10 294K/128.8/124.9/126.9 · schoolteacher-e5 304K/144.0/143.0/143.5 · schoolteacher-e6 296K/141.2/139.2/140.2 · schoolteacher-e7 294K/139.5/137.8/138.6 · schoolteacher-e8 289K/129.2/131.6/130.4 · schoolteacher-e9 287K/129.1/129.6/129.4 · schoolteacher-e10 280K/134.6/134.8/134.7 · preacher-e5 298K/135.0/130.4/132.7 · preacher-e6 284K/135.2/130.8/133.0 · preacher-e7 288K/131.4/128.4/129.9 · preacher-e8 289K/128.5/126.9/127.7 · preacher-e9 294K/131.4/129.6/130.5 · preacher-e10 287K/130.7/130.9/130.8 · salvage-king-e8 311K/127.1/129.3/128.2. **31/31 means inside row 60's accepted 124–145 (125.0–143.5) and 62/62 corners clear the 120 floor** — lowest corner 124.1 (clerk-e9 TR), highest 145.0 (newsie-e7 TL). The widest within-plate spread is **5.1** (clerk-e7), less than half row 74's 11.3, which is what chaining a reference does to consistency. **Largest processed-vs-raw corner drift is 0.20** with the corner window scaled 60→23 px alongside the 1024→384 downscale (newsie-e6, newsie-e9, schoolteacher-e7), so the downscale introduced nothing. **VERIFY-DON'T-INHERIT: all 36 raw statistics were re-measured here from the raws rather than read off `generation.jsonl`, and 36/36 agree with the log exactly** (the log records tl/tr/mean per accepted generation; every value above reproduces it). **FRAMING QA:** the card crops `object-fit: cover` into 74×90, so a square source is scaled by height and only X can move it. Ink centroid (luminance-weighted, weight = 255 − Rec.709 luma over all 147,456 px) for the thirty-one: **184.3–197.7 of 384** against the 56 registered plates' 185.9–198.5. The low end moves out by 1.6 px (tavernkeeper-e7 at 184.3) and the high end does not move (newsie-e6 at 197.7). That makes **tavernkeeper-e7 the widest deviation from centre in th